SUMMARY:FreeOnFriday? Hike - Governor Dick
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Bicycle Club (LBC) Meetup\nHike coordinator: Jan Zer
 foss 717-201-0530\n\n\\~5.5 miles. Blue 15 to yellow (horseshoe) 13-5-9-6-
 3 trails. Actual distance and route subject to change based on day-of weat
 her and trail conditions.\n\n[Governor Dick website](https://www.parkatgov
 ernordick.org/visit.html)\n[Alltrails](https://www.alltrails.com/trail/us/
 pennsylvania/governor-dick-outer-loop) We'll hike parts of this.\n\nThere 
 are portable toilet facilities in the parking lot. There should also be a 
 portable toilet midway.\n\nPlease bring your own water and energy snack an
 d first aid kit. I always strongly encourage bringing hiking poles. Please
  be sure to familiarize yourself with the route and terrain to make sure t
 his hike is within your capabilities.\n\nIt is hunting season so please re
 member to wear blaze orange or some other high viz clothing.\n\nAfter hike
  coffee/lunch: If we get done in time some of us may want to try getting i
 ndividual tables of 3-5 at the [Porch and Pantry](https://www.porchandpant
 ry.com/) in Mount Gretna. They close at 1:00. If that does not work out\, 
 some may wish to try [The Hideaway](https://www.mtgretnahideaway.com) in M
 ount Gretna or [Colebrook Tavern](https://colebrooktavern.com) in Colebroo
 k.\n\nTo eliminate passing around a pen and paper waiver\, we require LBC 
 Club membership and Meetup RSVP below to join this ride. Being on\nMeetup 
 does not mean you are a club member. Join here [Member Signup](https://www
 .lancasterbikeclub.net/content.aspx?page_id=60&club_id=257148)\n\nYour RSV
 P is your agreement to abide by the club's Code of Conduct: [Code of Condu
 ct](https://www.lancasterbikeclub.net/content.aspx?page_id=22&club_id=2571
 48&module_id=323984)\n\nGuidance if an incident occurs: [Incident Actions]
 (https://lancasterbikeclub.net/content.aspx?page_id=22&club_id=257148&modu
