SUMMARY:Ride the Pa Abandoned Turnpike 20 F
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Bicycle Club (LBC) Meetup\nJoin members and friends 
 of the Lancaster Bicycle Club and Rails for Trails for a bike ride through
  the abandoned tunnels of the Pennsylvania Turnpike. When the turnpike was
  expanded to go over the mountain at Breezewood\, three tunnels and a plaz
 a were abandoned. The trail is 10 miles long and flat.\n\nFrom Lancaster\n
 We will meet together\, leaving the parking lot of Walmart\, the 222 Ephra
 ta exit on Saturday morning\, November 21st at 8am. Use Meet Up comments t
 o make arrangements and please carpool. We will drive North one exit on 22
 2\, getting on the Turnpike and driving West to the Breezwood exit. This i
 s a 1 and ½ hour drive. After getting off the turnpike we will meet re-gr
 oup at the exit at Scheetz.\nFrom Maryland\nDrive directly to the in inter
 section of Rt. 30 and the Pa Turnpike exit at Breezwood. Everyone meeting 
 at Sheetz at 10am.\nThe entrance to the trail is 1/2 mile away\, route 30 
 and Tannery Road.\n\nCaution\n-since 1968 the trail has been abandoned. It
  is mostly gravel now.\n-no road bikes…\n-there are no lights in these t
 unnels. You must have bright front lights on you bicycles.\n-one tunnel is
  1 ½ mile long\, completely dark.\nAfter returning to Breezwood\, we will
  hang out and eat together at Bob Evan’s. Each rider will wear a helmet 
 and have a tube for you or someone to fix.\nRichard Conner\, leader\n717-5
 72-8480
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/lancaster-bicycle-club/events/3170785
 43/
